# Line endings, pinned. This repo's CI runs on windows-latest, and without a policy git checks out
# CRLF there while ubuntu and macos get LF — so any test that parses text with a hardcoded "\n"
# passes on two platforms and fails on the third.
#
# That is not hypothetical: CI run 33146510964 failed on windows-latest ONLY, in
# tests/integration_capability_envelope.rs, which locates a struct's end with find("\n}\n"). The
# test's own assertion was never reached on Windows, so its field allowlist had been guarding
# nothing there while reporting nothing wrong.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out LF everywhere. Rust, cargo and rustfmt are
# all indifferent to this; the tests are not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git must not touch them. A "line ending" inside a page image or a WAL fixture is data.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.wal binary
